# Responsive UI

Every section must work on phone (~360px), tablet (~768–1024), laptop (~1280), and large desktop (~1440+).

- Use `clamp()` for headings, not fixed `text-5xl` on small phones.
- Sticky `h-dvh` stages: content must fit without clipping. On short screens (`max-height: 740px`) shrink gaps, images, and lockets — never rely on `overflow-hidden` to hide copy.
- Pad with `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for notched phones.
- Stack layouts below `64rem`; side-by-side only on laptop+.
- Do not let decorative hearts, lanterns, or 3D canvas cover headings or CTAs.
- Test mentally at 360×740, 768×1024, 1280×800, and 1440×900 before finishing UI work.
- `overflow-x: hidden` on `body`; no element should force horizontal scroll.
